# Build products, regenerated by the probe that writes them.
#
# ⚠️ derived-truth-floor/ MUST be ignored rather than committed. music21 stamps a
# fresh 32-hex instrument id on every write, so these files are semantically
# deterministic and NOT byte-deterministic — committing them makes every re-run
# of probe_structural_floor.py show ~48 modified lines per file that mean
# nothing. The reproduction check that does work is the CANONICAL hash against
# benchmarks/omr-page-normalise-fixes-2026-09/derived-truth-bytes.json, which
# the probe performs and records in structural-floor-measured.json.
derived-truth-floor/
